Ruby on Rails Active Storage with the default vips image processor contains a critical remote-code-execution vulnerability. The flaw affects Rails 7.0.0–7.2.3.1 and 8.0.0–8.1.3 on default configurations, and Rails 6.0.0–6.1.7.10 only if Active Storage has been customized. The vulnerability requires untrusted image uploads and vips as the image processor.

The research team reports arbitrary file read and remote code execution as the application process user. Fixed versions are Rails 7.2.3.2, 8.0.5.1, and 8.1.3.1. The fix requires libvips 8.13 or later; upgrading Rails alone is insufficient if libvips is older. A stopgap is available: setting the VIPS_BLOCK_UNTRUSTED environment variable on libvips 8.13+ prevents exploitation.

Operators should verify their Rails version, patch immediately to the fixed releases, and ensure libvips is version 8.

